Hello netdev,

The Enhanced IP team (an alternative protocol to IPv6) now has a draft
RFC available.  We are looking for people who would be willing to be
co-authors on the RFC and possibly also contribute code for the Linux
implementation.  What is involved: at this point proof-reading the
document and signing your name next to ours. If you're interested, the
RFC and our IEEE Computer magazine paper is here:
          http://www.enhancedip.org/documentation.html

Our prototype kernel and userland code can be found here:
           http://www.enhancedip.org/code.html

If you're not sure iPv6 is the answer, please give our work a closer look.

Best Regards,

Sam Patton
